{"term":"mandarin","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:d98f958820bc22d205","definition":"A high government bureaucrat of the Chinese Empire.","example":"LIKE THE MANDARINS of old, the rulers of China live behind high walls. When they emerge, which they rarely do, they travel in cars with rear windows curtained like sedan chairs.\nThey live in the Chung Nan Hai, a walled park adjacent to the Forbidden City from where ancient dynasties ruled the Celestial Empire.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"historical","register":"historical","wordFamily":["Cleopatra mandarin","lemandarin","mandarinal","mandarinate","mandarin collar","mandarindom","mandariness","mandarin fish","mandarin gown","mandarinic","mandarining","mandarinism","mandarinize","mandarinquat","mandarinship","mandarin square"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mandarin#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:771e2691985bc18234","definition":"A pedantic or elitist bureaucrat.","example":"The mandarins who are managing this pandemic are fond of speaking of war.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["Cleopatra mandarin","lemandarin","mandarinal","mandarinate","mandarin collar","mandarindom","mandariness","mandarin fish","mandarin gown","mandarinic","mandarining","mandarinism","mandarinize","mandarinquat","mandarinship","mandarin square"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mandarin#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c6e44cc4c1a145e0c4","definition":"A pedantic senior person of influence in academia or literary circles.","example":"Its sting preserved to literature a fierce peculiar genius [Waugh] who, in the 40 years before his death last week at 62, achieved recognition as the grand old mandarin of modern British prose and as a satirist whose skill at sticking pens in people rates him a roomy cell in the murderers’ row (Swift, Pope, Wilde, Shaw) of English letters.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"derogatory, sometimes","register":"derogatory, sometimes","wordFamily":["Cleopatra mandarin","lemandarin","mandarinal","mandarinate","mandarin collar","mandarindom","mandariness","mandarin fish","mandarin gown","mandarinic","mandarining","mandarinism","mandarinize","mandarinquat","mandarinship","mandarin square"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mandarin#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:6314bb8f3fbeb52f19","definition":"Ellipsis of mandarin duck.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"abbreviation, alt-of, ellipsis","register":"abbreviation, alt-of, ellipsis","wordFamily":["Cleopatra mandarin","lemandarin","mandarinal","mandarinate","mandarin collar","mandarindom","mandariness","mandarin fish","mandarin gown","mandarinic","mandarining","mandarinism","mandarinize","mandarinquat","mandarinship","mandarin square"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mandarin#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b0bd6af02e1ed5d0de","definition":"A senior civil servant.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"UK, informal","register":"UK, informal","wordFamily":["Cleopatra mandarin","lemandarin","mandarinal","mandarinate","mandarin collar","mandarindom","mandariness","mandarin fish","mandarin gown","mandarinic","mandarining","mandarinism","mandarinize","mandarinquat","mandarinship","mandarin square"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mandarin#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:261665be9d9d95f0a7","definition":"A figurine of a Chinese person with movable head that was popular in the 1950s. (Cf. bobblehead.)","example":"He lay quietly in the hydropathic bed while his heart shuddered and his eyes focused at random on objects in the room, simulating a calm he could not feel. The walls of green jade, the nightlight in the porcelain mandarin whose head nodded interminably if you touched him, the multi-clock that radiated the time of three planets and six satellites, the bed itself, a crystal pool flowing with carbonated glycerine at ninety-nine point nine Fahrenheit.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["Cleopatra mandarin","lemandarin","mandarinal","mandarinate","mandarin collar","mandarindom","mandariness","mandarin fish","mandarin gown","mandarinic","mandarining","mandarinism","mandarinize","mandarinquat","mandarinship","mandarin square"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mandarin#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ed53911a961becbe2e","definition":"Pertaining to or reminiscent of mandarins; deliberately superior or complex; esoteric, highbrow, obscurantist.","example":"A mandarin impassivity had descended over Smiley's face. The earlier emotion was quite gone.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["Cleopatra mandarin","lemandarin","mandarinal","mandarinate","mandarin collar","mandarindom","mandariness","mandarin fish","mandarin gown","mandarinic","mandarining","mandarinism","mandarinize","mandarinquat","mandarinship","mandarin square"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mandarin#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:3e9401dab6b9eeb71b","definition":"Ellipsis of mandarin orange:","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["Cleopatra mandarin","lemandarin","mandarinal","mandarinate","mandarin collar","mandarindom","mandariness","mandarin fish","mandarin gown","mandarinic","mandarining","mandarinism","mandarinize","mandarinquat","mandarinship","mandarin square"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mandarin#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ec7f0d5c78b0c98b7c","definition":"An orange colour.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["Cleopatra mandarin","lemandarin","mandarinal","mandarinate","mandarin collar","mandarindom","mandariness","mandarin fish","mandarin gown","mandarinic","mandarining","mandarinism","mandarinize","mandarinquat","mandarinship","mandarin square"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mandarin#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:7b0d03ad35e5eb3c18","definition":"Standard Mandarin, an official language of China and Taiwan, and one of four official languages in Singapore; Putonghua, Guoyu or Huayu.","example":"[...]and though the ſame word hath one ſignification in the Mandorines Language, and a contrary in Japan and other places, yet knowing one Speech and their Character, you may Travel not only through the Empire of China, but the adjacent Kingdoms.","pos":"name","synonyms":["Beifanghua","Guanhua","Guoyu","Huayu","Mandarin Chinese","Putonghua","Standard Chinese","Standard Mandarin","Standard Spoken Chinese"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["Cleopatra mandarin","lemandarin","mandarinal","mandarinate","mandarin collar","mandarindom","mandariness","mandarin fish","mandarin gown","mandarinic","mandarining","mandarinism","mandarinize","mandarinquat","mandarinship","mandarin square"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Mandarin#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:bd3e59f2b6a1d39218","definition":"A branch of the Chinese languages, consisting of many dialects; Guanhua or Beifanghua.","example":"\"Two, three, four, five, south! Six, seven, eight, nine, north!\" Strange as it may sound, this is the way the people on the Chinese mainland complain about the lack of clothes, food and other necessities.\nAbsent from the phrases are \"one\" and \"ten\"—\"i\" and \"shih\" in Chinese Mandarin. The words for \"clothes\" and \"food\" sound alike. Also missing are \"east\" and \"west.\" Their Chinese equivalents when put together as \"tung-hsi,\" stand for \"things,\" \"objects\" or \"matters.\"","pos":"name","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["Cleopatra mandarin","lemandarin","mandarinal","mandarinate","mandarin collar","mandarindom","mandariness","mandarin fish","mandarin gown","mandarinic","mandarining","mandarinism","mandarinize","mandarinquat","mandarinship","mandarin square"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Mandarin#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/ˈmæn.də.ɹɪn/","us":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/1/15/En-us-mandarin.ogg/En-us-mandarin.ogg.mp3"},"wordFamily":["Cleopatra mandarin","lemandarin","mandarinal","mandarinate","mandarin collar","mandarindom","mandariness","mandarin fish","mandarin gown","mandarinic","mandarining","mandarinism","mandarinize","mandarinquat","mandarinship","mandarin square"]}